  "content": {
    "title": "The Masters is 50 days out. What you need to know about 90th edition",
    "text": "Feb. 18, 2026, 8:01 a.m. ETThe calendar says it's Feb. 18 but a closer look reveals that we are now 50 days out from the 2026 Masters.The first men's major of the year is the best major of the year, according to many a golf fan. The 2026 rendition will be the 90th playing of the tournament that was called the Augusta National Invitational Tournament when it first started.Here's what you need to know about the 2026 Masters.When is the 2026 Masters?Masters Week starts with Monday and Tuesday practice rounds on April 6-7. The Par 3 Contest is Wednesday, April 8. The first round of the Masters is Thursday, April 9, and the final round will be Sunday, April 12.Who's playing in the 2026 Masters?The field is still coming together but a good portion of it is already known. There are more than two dozen ways to qualify for the Masters, and while the Augusta National Golf Club has extended special invitations to some golfers in the past, and there have been modifications made to the qualification criteria over the years, many of the ways that players earn a \"golden ticket\" have not changed. Winners of PGA Tour events between now and then can still earn a spot.Is Tiger Woods playing in the 2026 Masters?Mark it down as a maybe. Ahead of the Genesis Invitational, he said he's been hitting full shots, but still doesn’t have a target date for his return to competition after undergoing disc replacement surgery in October.But when asked if the Masters in April is off the table, Woods didn’t hesitate: “No,” he said and smiled a sly smile. How many amateurs have qualified for the Masters?Six amateurs have locked up their spots for Augusta National, and that should complete the amateur portion of the field, barring Augusta National deciding to offer any special invites (or an amateur wins a PGA Tour event between now and then). Michael La Sasso had a spot in the Masters but gave it up when he signed with LIV Golf.Where is the Masters played?That would, of course, be Augusta National Golf Club, which first held the tournament in 1934. Since 1940, the tournament is scheduled for the first full week of April. It's the only one of the four men's majors to be played at the same golf course every year.Who is the defending champion at the Masters?Rory McIlroy completed the career grand slam, and won his first major in 11 years, when he outlasted Justin Rose at the 2025 Masters.How do you get tickets to the Masters?Every June 1, Augusta National opens its ticket application process for the next year. The 2026 tickets have all been allocated. Golf fans will find several options for tickets on the secondary exchanges but:As a reminder, Augusta National, Inc. is the only authorized source/seller of Masters® Tickets. The resale of any Masters Ticket is strictly prohibited. Holders of Tickets acquired from third parties, by whatever means, may be excluded from attendance to the Tournament.How to watch the 2026 MastersESPN and CBS are joined this year by Amazon Prime Video, which will have early round coverage on Thursday and Friday for the first time in 2026. There is also a multitude of viewing options on the official Masters website and app, with a variety of featured holes and featured groups each day of the competition.",
